         <pb/>
         <div type="div1">
            <head>Lycanthropus</head>
            <p rend="justify">Proofreading Team at https://www.pgdp.net</p>
            <p rend="justify">Lycanthropus</p>
            <p rend="justify">By C. EDGAR BOLEN</p>
            <lg>
               <l>  The jellied night has oozed its miry black</l>
               <l>    From out the hills to fill the valley floor.</l>
               <l>  Atop the ragged hills the torn cloud-wrack</l>
               <l>    Is lightning-limned into a hellish door.</l>
               <l>      A gust of wind across the sky is hurled—</l>
               <l>      The gods of old are loosed upon the world.</l>
            </lg>
            <lg>
               <l>  Age-old, the blood-lust wells within my throat;</l>
               <l>    Tensely I wait, and feel my body shrink;</l>
               <l>  My hairless hide becomes a furry coat.</l>
               <l>    Blood-hungry, through the opened door I slink;</l>
               <l>      I raise my head and howl in horrid glee—</l>
               <l>      And from the plain a howl comes back to me.</l>
            </lg>
            <p rend="justify">TRANSCRIBER'S NOTE: This etext was produced from Weird Tales August-September 1936. Extensive research did not uncover any evidence that the U.S. copyright on this publication was renewed.</p>
         </div>
